From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VyOS LS1046A <ask20@vyos-ls1046a-build>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dpaa: bound the ingress CGR by frames, not bytes (0178)

The ingress congestion group counted bytes up to 256 MB, so a flood the CPU
cannot keep up with held the port's whole RX buffer pool before the group
tripped, and FMan then discarded everything the port received, offloaded
flows included (HW-reproduced 2026-10-28: 9.4 Gbit/s offloaded flow fell to 0
under a ~2 Mpps pktgen flood). Count frames at ingress_quarters/4 (default 2)
of the port's pool seed (config_count x possible CPUs), vendor patch 111.
plans/ASK2-VENDOR-ASK-REVIEW.md R5.

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
index 3edc8d1..08e96ef 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
@@ -66,12 +66,10 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(tx_timeout, "The Tx timeout in ms");
 			  NETIF_MSG_LINK | NETIF_MSG_IFUP | \
 			  NETIF_MSG_IFDOWN | NETIF_MSG_HW)
 
-#define DPAA_INGRESS_CS_THRESHOLD 0x10000000
-/* Ingress congestion threshold on FMan ports
- * The size in bytes of the ingress tail-drop threshold on FMan ports.
- * Traffic piling up above this value will be rejected by QMan and discarded
- * by FMan.
- */
+static uint dpaa_ingress_quarters = 2;
+module_param_named(ingress_quarters, dpaa_ingress_quarters, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(ingress_quarters,
+		 "Quarters of a port's pool seed its queues to the CPU may hold (1-4)");
 
 /* Size in bytes of the FQ taildrop threshold */
 #define DPAA_FQ_TD 0x200000
@@ -3227,6 +3225,13 @@ static struct dpaa_bp *dpaa_bp_alloc(struct device *dev)
  * We won't be sending congestion notifications to FMan; for now, we just use
  * this CGR to generate enqueue rejections to FMan in order to drop the frames
  * before they reach our ingress queues and eat up memory.
+ *
+ * A frame waiting on these queues for the CPU holds a buffer of the port's
+ * pool, and only the CPU taking it puts one back. The group used to count
+ * bytes up to 256 MB, which a flood the CPU cannot keep up with never reaches
+ * before the pool is empty, so FMan then discards everything the port
+ * receives, hardware-forwarded frames included. Count frames instead, at
+ * ingress_quarters/4 of what the port seeds its pool with.
  */
 static int dpaa_ingress_cgr_init(struct dpaa_priv *priv)
 {
@@ -3243,9 +3248,12 @@ static int dpaa_ingress_cgr_init(struct dpaa_priv *priv)
 
 	/* Enable CS TD, but disable Congestion State Change Notifications. */
 	memset(&initcgr, 0, sizeof(initcgr));
-	initcgr.we_mask = cpu_to_be16(QM_CGR_WE_CS_THRES);
-	initcgr.cgr.cscn_en = QM_CGR_EN;
-	cs_th = DPAA_INGRESS_CS_THRESHOLD;
+	initcgr.we_mask = cpu_to_be16(QM_CGR_WE_MODE | QM_CGR_WE_CS_THRES |
+				     QM_CGR_WE_CSCN_EN);
+	initcgr.cgr.mode = QMAN_CGR_MODE_FRAME;
+	initcgr.cgr.cscn_en = 0;
+	cs_th = max_t(u32, priv->dpaa_bp->config_count * num_possible_cpus() *
+			   clamp_t(uint, dpaa_ingress_quarters, 1, 4) / 4, 1);
 	qm_cgr_cs_thres_set64(&initcgr.cgr.cs_thres, cs_th, 1);
 
 	initcgr.we_mask |= cpu_to_be16(QM_CGR_WE_CSTD_EN);
